Resolve the graph ownership lock root through os.homedir().

deps/graph-lifecycle/ownership.cjs runtimeRoot() derives the runtime-locks
directory from os.userInfo().homedir. Node documents that field as coming from
the operating system password file, unlike os.homedir(), which consults the HOME
environment variable first and only falls back to the password entry. Every
other home lookup in the tree uses os.homedir(), including index.cjs in this
same deps/graph-lifecycle package (line 52, tilde expansion for the root dir),
logseq.cli.root-dir/default-root-dir, and frontend.worker.platform.node, so
ownership.cjs is the sole place where an exported HOME is ignored.

That divergence breaks any caller that relocates HOME, because acquireOwnership
mkdirs runtimeRoot() before it opens lock.sqlite. In the Nix build sandbox on
Darwin the build user's password entry points at /var/empty, so the checks fail
with

  Error (server-cleanup-failed): EACCES: permission denied, mkdir
  '/var/empty/Library/Application Support/Logseq/runtime-locks/<hash>'

even though the check exports HOME to a writable directory. Linux escapes it
only by accident: the Linux sandbox's synthetic passwd entry already points at
the writable build directory, so both lookups agree there. The same divergence
hits any sandbox, container, CI runner, or multi-user setup that sets HOME to
something other than the password-file value.

Fix: call os.homedir() in runtimeRoot(). This keeps the password entry as the
fallback for callers with no HOME set, so behavior is unchanged when HOME
matches the passwd value, and it makes the ownership root agree with the root
dir that the rest of the CLI already resolves through os.homedir().

Removal condition: drop this patch when upstream resolves the ownership runtime
root through os.homedir() (or another HOME-aware lookup) in
deps/graph-lifecycle/ownership.cjs. A failed strict apply in the nightly build
or the CLI build is the drift signal.

diff --git a/deps/graph-lifecycle/ownership.cjs b/deps/graph-lifecycle/ownership.cjs
--- a/deps/graph-lifecycle/ownership.cjs
+++ b/deps/graph-lifecycle/ownership.cjs
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
 const crypto = require('node:crypto');

 function runtimeRoot() {
-  const home = os.userInfo().homedir;
+  const home = os.homedir();
   switch (process.platform) {
     case 'darwin': return path.join(home, 'Library', 'Application Support', 'Logseq', 'runtime-locks');
     case 'win32': return path.join(home, 'AppData', 'Local', 'Logseq', 'runtime-locks');
